  "title": "May Thirtieth Movement",
  "summary": "On 30 May 1925 police in Shanghai's International Settlement opened fire on a demonstration on Nanjing Road, killing 13. The shooting, which followed the killing of the mill worker Gu Zhenghong, set off strikes, boycotts and anti-imperialist protests across China.",
